==English==
===Etymology===
{{etyl|grc|en}} [[Λάμια]].  From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|λαιμός||gullet|tr=laimos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|Greek mythology|lang=en}} A [[monster]] with the head and breasts of a woman and the lower half of a serpent, which ate children and sucked the [[blood]] from men.
# {{context|Greek mythology|lang=en}} A [[creature]] that feeds on blood.  

